// Title: Audio Capture via PowerShell
// Sigma ID: 932fb0d8-692b-4b0f-a26e-5643a50fe7d6
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: E.M. Anhaus (originally from Atomic Blue Detections, Endgame), oscd.community, Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2019-10-24 | Modified: 2023-04-06
// ATT&CK: collection, T1123
// Description: Detects audio capture via PowerShell Cmdlet.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate audio capture by legitimate user.
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1123/T1123.md
//   - https://eqllib.readthedocs.io/en/latest/analytics/ab7a6ef4-0983-4275-a4f1-5c6bd3c31c23.html
//   - https://github.com/frgnca/AudioDeviceCmdlets
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_powershell_audio_capture.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "WindowsAudioDevice-Powershell-Cmdlet" or ProcessCommandLine contains "Toggle-AudioDevice" or ProcessCommandLine contains "Get-AudioDevice " or ProcessCommandLine contains "Set-AudioDevice " or ProcessCommandLine contains "Write-AudioDevice "
